# Category slugs renamed when the taxonomy landed: "audio" became "av"
# (speakerphones AND cameras) and "video" became "display" (monitors, LFD, IFP,
# LED). The two cameras moved category at the same time, so they need their own
# rules BEFORE the catch-all for their old parent — _redirects matches in file
# order, and /video/* would otherwise swallow them into /display.
/video/pro-web-camera   /av/pro-web-camera    301
/video/pro-ptz-camera   /av/pro-ptz-camera    301
/audio/*                /av/:splat            301
/video/*                /display/:splat       301
/audio                  /av                   301
/video                  /display              301

# SPA fallback: react-router owns every route, so unknown paths must return the
# shell rather than a 404.
#
# /api/** never reaches this. Pages runs Functions before _redirects and static
# assets, and functions/api/[[path]].js matches that prefix.
#
# Deliberately NOT a wildcard proxy: an over-broad rule here is how asset
# requests end up served as HTML - the exact failure now live on the Emergent
# deployment, where every reveal frame returns text/html with status 200.
/*    /index.html   200
